== V5 several ends: git's octopus precedent, and one merge state with two MERGE_HEADs
   git merge a b: exit 2; HEAD moved? False; MERGE_HEAD lines=0; status=[]
      Trying simple merge with a | Simple merge did not work, trying automatic merge. | Auto-merging src/x.c | Automated merge did not work. | Should not be doing an octopus. | ERROR: content conflict in src/x.c | fatal: merge program failed | Merge with strategy octopus failed.
   git merge b a: exit 1; HEAD moved? False; MERGE_HEAD lines=2; status=['UU src/x.c', 'M  src/y.c']
      Trying simple merge with b | Trying simple merge with a | Simple merge did not work, trying automatic merge. | Auto-merging src/x.c | Automatic merge failed; fix conflicts and then commit the result. | ERROR: content conflict in src/x.c | fatal: merge program failed
   -- plumbing: merge b cleanly, then a with a conflict, one state, MERGE_HEAD = b1 a1
      second step merge-tree exit 1: ['src/x.c', 'Auto-merging', 'src/x.c', 'CONFLICT', '(content):', 'Merge', 'conflict', 'in', 'src/x.c']
      status: ['UU src/x.c', 'M  src/y.c']  HEAD still H? True
      after merge --abort: HEAD=H status=[] MERGE_HEAD? False
